# Portfolio Project Guidelines

React + TypeScript + Vite using Tailwind CSS v4, Three.js (R3F), GSAP, Framer Motion, and Supabase.

## Stack

- React 19, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`)
- 3D: `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei` under `src/components/backgrounds/three/`
- Animation: GSAP, Framer Motion; 2D particles via `tsparticles`
- Data: Supabase (`src/lib/supabase.ts`); icons: `lucide-react`; routing: `react-router-dom`

## Architecture

- `src/components/` — UI by area (`backgrounds/`, `ui/`, `admin/`)
- `src/pages/` — route components
- `src/lib/` — utilities, `AnimationContext`, `AnimationOrchestrator`, Supabase clients
- `src/hooks/<responsibility>/` — reusable hooks (never inside component folders)
- `src/styles/` — shared CSS by responsibility

## Build & Validate

```bash
npm run dev    # development
npm run lint   # 0 errors required
npm run build  # tsc -b && vite build
```

## Zero-Tolerance Rules

- No duplication — extract to `src/lib/` or shared components/hooks/CSS
- No `any`, `@ts-nocheck`, bare `catch (e) {}`, or silent failures
- No workaround typings when `@types/*` or canonical package types exist — use `src/types/` aliases when needed
- No `console.log/debug/info` — only `console.error/warn` for system failures
- Unused vars → prefix `_` or remove; complete hook dependency arrays
- Async/await only — never `.then()/.catch()` chains

